{"title":"2018 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A convex quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/a/84aef7a5215eb3e07d1b570f35d15c1a39f87762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\cdot CD=BC \\cdot DA.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"174\" height=\"14\" /> Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies inside\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> so that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/678580eb739fa31d055954e4e3a21dd033f345a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XAB = \\angle XCD$\" width=\"140\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d43fcb0ebed046e4ce49e69d78d93a2fd889607.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XBC = \\angle XDA.$\" width=\"144\" height=\"13\" />\nProve that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47e7a6d8f00d5693e0d9c9b60be6b8db86c9fe6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BXA + \\angle DXC = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"196\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2018_IMO_6bb.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/57/2018_IMO_6bb.png/470px-2018_IMO_6bb.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"470\" height=\"214\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/57/2018_IMO_6bb.png/705px-2018_IMO_6bb.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/57/2018_IMO_6bb.png/940px-2018_IMO_6bb.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2018_IMO_6.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/d2/2018_IMO_6.png/470px-2018_IMO_6.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"470\" height=\"236\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/d2/2018_IMO_6.png/705px-2018_IMO_6.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/d2/2018_IMO_6.png/940px-2018_IMO_6.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2018_IMO_6e.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8a/2018_IMO_6e.png/470px-2018_IMO_6e.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"470\" height=\"257\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8a/2018_IMO_6e.png/705px-2018_IMO_6e.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8a/2018_IMO_6e.png/940px-2018_IMO_6e.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>We want to find the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87fa832bf21ebc48a46289cd7aea73ffcc84c111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbc7892b9acc4ec136a9946aadb6c0f15ff1ed41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfaf1de1cd821c3c1698072f3cd91d4594ad9b14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> respectively.\nThe poinx <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/42501e1c7100f340da9bd452bf942219ac6b131b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> so points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/0993044565c8c1da708ba4ef5e2c312cc9f5991a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E,A,X,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> follow in this order.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/f/30f945c2e6fc84e7c58d753f8b2cb8fa28d9a4a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XAB =  \\angle XCD \\implies  \\angle XAE +  \\angle XCE = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"389\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd1ffaac5b468cd0749e5f4232e53aec3a47b3ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies AXCE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/732541a08db1c378df9512dbf09a22cf2eef3f0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies X$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> lie on circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/ddd20363040bba06b346a4d8346c641788d46402.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACE.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lie on circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f443783893c37ed353183ce3c0911a15f254ad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the point of intersection of circles  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f348b5890100fa57eaa4a3c548badc83b75af585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c55f6ad39f1f1c6266571bef0ef26b41d1820552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega = BDF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Special case</b></i>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d4764b1f8fc63a3850fdb7135d4a47e291e3410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/3/523ba8026a994f2cc5cc0fa260527262104c12a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = BC \\implies  AB \\cdot CD = BC \\cdot DA.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"305\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are symmetric with respect to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/7/497c313ae21274a99213b7fa622b86c9818f79ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = ACEF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" /> <i><b>(Claim 1).</b></i>\n</p><p>The circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b93a2dc17d4cf5e91cf1edaa02b2a16f690e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is orthogonal to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <i><b>(Claim 2).</b></i>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e931d8d6ffd32ed06cb7d19ad02eddc8bd1080.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hspace{10mm} \\angle FCX =  \\angle BCX  =  \\frac {\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {XAF}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"262\" height=\"49\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/6/79607326260cf94d825a16e94c1c1b1a8af24db6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a282fc4517aec12bf66df39246dfa2622699deba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hspace{10mm} \\angle CBX = \\angle XDA =  \\frac {\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {XBF}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"264\" height=\"49\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de82b5de37f029271b42d807a7a35ac5a7e8e7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/8978fa72ca225c09843eab5c1c2c48ba9f367446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {XAF} + \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {XBF} = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"173\" height=\"25\" />  <i><b>(Claim 3)</b></i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef48ac956824fcaea163a530a717e6df694aa006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"9\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce52e954334f8ca5ed87d208676f1cc98f7240fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XCB + \\angle XBC = 90^\\circ \\implies \\angle CXB = 90^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"354\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/813331bf3809fd11a4eb1b1d7d304d3b60e1adee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AXD =  90^\\circ \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"155\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/409378bad796b7b7dfe8d3c184a4e22dae236bc7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BXA + \\angle DXC = 360^\\circ -\\angle AXD -\\angle CXB = 180^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"421\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2018_IMO_6c.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/86/2018_IMO_6c.png/470px-2018_IMO_6c.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"470\" height=\"238\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/86/2018_IMO_6c.png/705px-2018_IMO_6c.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/86/2018_IMO_6c.png/940px-2018_IMO_6c.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2018_IMO_6d.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/49/2018_IMO_6d.png/470px-2018_IMO_6d.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"470\" height=\"225\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/49/2018_IMO_6d.png/705px-2018_IMO_6d.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/49/2018_IMO_6d.png/940px-2018_IMO_6d.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><i><b>Common case </b></i>\n</p><p>Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the intersection point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a0b75202202b36c2a62a22bba07fc06501bea7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be a circle (red) with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b34dea98f1dcf14a3522fcb374da939c9178b3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA = R.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>We will prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/2/7b284a977f0ac793fd60deb95c61f52be39c8d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\angle BXA =\\sin \\angle DXC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"194\" height=\"14\" /> using point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> symmetric to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39ff5eebd99794acd0068ae889b1498d54ececd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" /> \n</p><p>The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are symmetric with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> <i><b>(Claim 1).</b></i>\n</p><p>The circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b93a2dc17d4cf5e91cf1edaa02b2a16f690e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96e81e1599a08776bb0799f73128f99332c1d78f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> are orthogonal to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> <i><b>(Claim 2).</b></i>\n</p><p>Circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d26814d18c58880c417c280a1be37350be9c57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACF$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f348b5890100fa57eaa4a3c548badc83b75af585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> are symmetric with respect to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> <i><b>(Lemma).</b></i>\n</p><p>Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the point of intersection of circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b93a2dc17d4cf5e91cf1edaa02b2a16f690e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/f/e7ff4903a0c91647d95fc9222a1b7de920a454d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACF.$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Quadrangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95f0c893bb5b2495323d5578473cb5e0eb443b40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BYDF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47be676753b3fb920fa2ef3932b4b1b2d1853b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies  \\angle CBY =  \\angle ADY.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"186\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Quadrangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d59b7475d1808c7581a1fb0d98141380f8ea7d83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AYCF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/b/b1b9a6795a6c8c4682db4e46e0eea3c00a767b33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies  \\angle YAD = \\angle YCB.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"189\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p>The triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/c/53cdc8a2132e477162b232a6a801f8901304b0c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle YAD \\sim \\triangle YCB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> by two angles, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/7/347428161366f9e30abb38cb52d2947c2f4b8c37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {BC}{AD} = \\frac {CY}{AY} = \\frac {BY} {DY} \\hspace{10mm} (1).\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are symmetric with respect to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, since they lie on the intersection of the circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d26814d18c58880c417c280a1be37350be9c57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACF$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f348b5890100fa57eaa4a3c548badc83b75af585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> symmetric with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and the  circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b93a2dc17d4cf5e91cf1edaa02b2a16f690e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> orthogonal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39ff5eebd99794acd0068ae889b1498d54ececd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" />\n</p><p>The point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is symmetric to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36faaec0a935bfb0e7247bdf7cdd86f66c076661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f54aa7a7cab8016db399fc0363ce1523b1091477.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\triangle OBC \\sim \\triangle OCD \\implies \\frac {OB}{OC} = \\frac {BC}{CD} = \\frac {OC}{OD},\\]\" width=\"346\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9f872be60f7ae8bd566992123d1ac739ceefbd9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {OB}{OD} = \\frac {OB}{OC} \\cdot \\frac {OC}{OD} = \\frac{BC^2}{CD^2} = \\frac{BC}{CD} \\cdot \\frac {AB}{AD}.\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"39\" />\nThe point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is symmetric to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is symmetric to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dcdcd9c8cdbd7c4679fd83fca62a617ba3727fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> hence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/8/3d8e114de68a65856f7df10b7c8b2a272575fe60.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {BX}{DY} = \\frac {R^2}{OD \\cdot OY} ,\\frac {DX}{BY} = \\frac{R^2}{OB \\cdot OY}.\\]\" width=\"280\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/606f2dbcdb98a31ec76d9b098095556987d08384.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{BX}{DX} =\\frac{DY}{BY} \\cdot \\frac {OB}{OD} = \\frac{AD}{BC} \\cdot \\frac{BC}{CD} \\cdot \\frac{AB}{AD} = \\frac{AB}{CD}.\\]\" width=\"351\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2018_IMO_6_angles.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9e/2018_IMO_6_angles.png/390px-2018_IMO_6_angles.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"390\" height=\"302\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/9/9e/2018_IMO_6_angles.png 1.5x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2018_IMO_6_Claim_3.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/38/2018_IMO_6_Claim_3.png/390px-2018_IMO_6_Claim_3.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"390\" height=\"269\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/38/2018_IMO_6_Claim_3.png/585px-2018_IMO_6_Claim_3.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/38/2018_IMO_6_Claim_3.png/780px-2018_IMO_6_Claim_3.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2018_IMO_6a.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4e/2018_IMO_6a.png/390px-2018_IMO_6a.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"390\" height=\"215\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4e/2018_IMO_6a.png/585px-2018_IMO_6a.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4e/2018_IMO_6a.png/780px-2018_IMO_6a.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Denote  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/b/e7be65434e28bab3ca481e40788dcd8f83af2578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XAB =  \\angle XCD = \\alpha,  \\angle BXA = \\varphi,   \\angle DXC = \\psi.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"390\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>By the law of sines for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/553421523e9f1ac5dff46d20b339146f5a6aeff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABX,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/5/c1510542e74294f7a8b0fc32f97195abd4a94060.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {AB}{\\sin \\varphi} = \\frac{BX}{\\sin \\alpha}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"113\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>By the law of sines for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e977d6c99ca50c4039fbeac9f0a8552f963f193.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDX,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" /> we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d6e533cdca0e0319ddc4fcc0fa6b5df188c208.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {CD}{\\sin \\psi} = \\frac {DX}{\\sin \\alpha}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"114\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Hence we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87f6e67993474c52cdb8a7ecc7525dd47a668d70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sin \\psi} {\\sin \\varphi}= \\frac {CD}{DX}  \\cdot \\frac{BX}{AB} = 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"191\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/1/a71843bee9946ff89d50ea241f9d10db52075f65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi = \\psi,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/725bdfa5a768fb0bd99148e231b0dba879528100.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle XAB \\sim  \\triangle XCD \\implies \\frac {CD}{AB} = \\frac {BX}{DX} = \\frac{AX}{CX} = \\frac {AD}{BC}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"415\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/0/490521ed0b1de1adcb18be9963a830ca023a995d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD \\cdot BC = AB \\cdot AD \\implies AD = CD, AB = BC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"395\" height=\"18\" /> This is a special case. \n</p><p>In all other cases, the equality of the sines follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249d1f9a1cbbc5d49301929a23c5842492498ec8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi + \\psi = 180^\\circ .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Claim 1</b></i> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb0b8e31ad2fe86bbca5d407f5f14709736f733.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be arbitrary points on a circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b0a237aa2a7e5ee7dbf6a32f406c9a6ba0b1630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega, l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> be the perpendicular bisector to the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a0b75202202b36c2a62a22bba07fc06501bea7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> Then the straight lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> at the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d115d4b1a9fe1fd995dc34e4525de65e85530d63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" /> symmetric with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39ff5eebd99794acd0068ae889b1498d54ececd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Claim 2</b></i> Let points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be symmetric with respect to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39ff5eebd99794acd0068ae889b1498d54ececd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" /> Then any circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> passing through these points is orthogonal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39ff5eebd99794acd0068ae889b1498d54ececd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Claim 3</b></i> The sum of the arcs between the points of intersection of two perpendicular circles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbe5fe997b97dbc059b8575ca1865621f346852a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />\nIn the figure they are a blue and red arcs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e66a7634891ffe9f94360ed1df5df08546ad30b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {CD}, \\alpha + \\beta = 180^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"27\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Lemma</b></i> The opposite sides of the quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />). The circle  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> centered at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> contains the ends of the diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a0b75202202b36c2a62a22bba07fc06501bea7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are symmetric with respect to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> (in other words, the inversion with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> maps <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62bd7c057061cb95f8a69b259ee60ec5534663de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> Then the circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f348b5890100fa57eaa4a3c548badc83b75af585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d26814d18c58880c417c280a1be37350be9c57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACF$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> are symmetric with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39ff5eebd99794acd0068ae889b1498d54ececd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>  We will prove that the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195d683ae02c57abf49ebe0889c6f2ea7bcc513e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> symmetric to the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dcdcd9c8cdbd7c4679fd83fca62a617ba3727fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> belongs to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d26814d18c58880c417c280a1be37350be9c57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACF$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> becouse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6cfadccba4a976cad4b784e9bd8d4b18934849e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AGC = \\angle AFC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>A circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96e81e1599a08776bb0799f73128f99332c1d78f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> containing points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> symmetric with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dcdcd9c8cdbd7c4679fd83fca62a617ba3727fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is orthogonal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> <i><b>(Claim 2)</b></i> and maps into itself under inversion with respect to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39ff5eebd99794acd0068ae889b1498d54ececd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" /> Hence, the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> under this inversion passes to some point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195d683ae02c57abf49ebe0889c6f2ea7bcc513e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> of the same circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/6/4a60c3d3e951fc039c01ee9fc9dc038f37f5bbb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDE.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>A straight line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> containing the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> of the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dcdcd9c8cdbd7c4679fd83fca62a617ba3727fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> under inversion with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dcdcd9c8cdbd7c4679fd83fca62a617ba3727fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> maps into the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a999bc4f8445db7f97d8691c09edb082f2265575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OADG.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> Hence, the inscribed angles of this circle are equal  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e157bbadbfc0123bc997b55609597ba31d5821c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADB =  \\angle AGE.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"143\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/207d6278ef1cdc707809f155438a5e0974377ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OCE =  \\angle CGE (CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" /> maps into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd9a921942267b80bd1d43a87e4d73a79c131d2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CG)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> and  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0f25f7a1b051a8ee161b140e8fc28b03e9be07c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OCE =  \\angle BCD (BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" /> maps into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d1c70e63035c3588b65650cd6c41cceb4198f98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> \nConsequently, the angles   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93ad678197b8d910a220fe6a7a8f50325022d7c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AFC =  \\angle ADB –  \\angle FBD = \\angle AGE -  \\angle CGE =  \\angle AGC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"446\" height=\"16\" />\nThese angles subtend the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/356ade0c1e7dad30f160bf94c214b58271040399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"24\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d26814d18c58880c417c280a1be37350be9c57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACF$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> circle, that is, the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195d683ae02c57abf49ebe0889c6f2ea7bcc513e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> symmetric to the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dcdcd9c8cdbd7c4679fd83fca62a617ba3727fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> belongs to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/f/e7ff4903a0c91647d95fc9222a1b7de920a454d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACF.$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO\" title=\"2018 IMO\">2018 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2018 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IM